WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
Vesicoureteral reflux reverses the
normal direction of urinary flow.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.600
Begin at the bladder and identify where each ureter

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:07.910
enters.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.340
The normal junction helps
prevent urine from moving backward

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:12.525
during bladder emptying.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.980
In reflux, a congenital
junction abnormality or abnormal ureteral

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.760
insertion can allow urine to travel back toward the

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:21.680
ureter and kidney.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.683
Watch the direction change along the same anatomy.

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.716
When the bladder urine is infected, reflux can carry

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.937
that infection upward
and encourage repeated pyelonephritis.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:36.100
The supplied chapter describes silent cases as well as

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.860
recurrent urinary infections, unexplained
fever, and poor growth.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.673
It lists prompt treatment
of infection and intervention for

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:45.273
recurrent or high-grade reflux.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.570
This visualization shows the
direction and consequence of reflux.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.573
It does not invent
the missing grade-by-grade criteria, and

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.829
its flow speed and volume are schematic.
